Others have already given good advice, but one thing I've noticed is
missing, which I consider to be key:

Take notes.

It used to be that I'd just plunge into the dungeon, figuring that I'd
figure out what things are through ID scrolls, etc., and that I could
remember where anything important was.  Then I started taking notes,
comparing prices (there are guides out there on what things cost, and the
markup/markdown system the shops use), and ascended that character.  Of
course, taking notes does not guarantee an ascension, but it really, really,
really helps.

Another point that helped me is that you don't need to "clear out" a branch.
I used to feel that I needed to go all the way through the mines before
continuing on in the dungeon, but that's asking for pain.  Take your
time--go down to minetown, then go back up and do Sokoban, and then go back
to reach the end of the mine, or something like--it's amazing what a
difference it can make.

